# Paint keys on paper, 256x128, fill and stroke forms. Left to right, top to bottom:
# (1) circle r18 with fill:p.red only: red disc, no outline. (2) circle r18 with fill:none stroke:p.ink,4: a ring of ink
# 4px thick, paper showing through the middle. (3) circle r18 with fill:p.gold and stroke:p.ink,6: gold disc with a
# thick 6px ink outline.
# (4) circle r18 with fill:p.green stroke:3 (width only): the ring is 3px of dark green, line(p.green), not ink and not
# the fill green; the inside is p.green.
# Bottom row: (5) circle r18 filled blue with blur:6: a soft disc with fuzzy edge, no crisp boundary. (6) the same
# circle with blur:0, crisp edge, for contrast. (7) a green 40x40 rect with name:j1 jitter:1.5,60: the outline is
# visibly wobbly, not a straight-sided square: amplitude 1.5px, wavelength 60px, so the edges bend in a few gentle
# curves. (8) the same rect with name:j2 jitter:3,12: amplitude 3px, wavelength 12px, so the outline is visibly rougher
# than cell 7, with a ragged edge of many short bumps, up to 3px off a straight side.
@target shapes/paint.png 256x128

circle 18 at:32,32 fill:p.red
circle 18 at:96,32 fill:none stroke:p.ink,4
circle 18 at:160,32 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,6
circle 18 at:224,32 fill:p.green stroke:3
circle 18 at:32,96 fill:p.blue blur:6
circle 18 at:96,96 fill:p.blue blur:0
rect 40x40 at:160,96 fill:p.green name:j1 jitter:1.5,60
rect 40x40 at:224,96 fill:p.green name:j2 jitter:3,12
